    "problem_statement": "Check constructor swaps instance_of and type arguments\n\n#### Description\n\nThe Check constructor appears to have swapped the `instance_of` and `type` arguments internally, causing validation to fail when using these parameters.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom glom import glom, Check, SKIP\n\n# This should work but fails\ntarget = [1, 'a']\nresult = glom(target, [Check(type=str, default=SKIP)])\nprint(\"Result:\", result)  # Expected: ['a'], but gets []\n\n# This also fails when it should work\nresult = glom(target, [Check(instance_of=str, default=SKIP)])\nprint(\"Result:\", result)  # Expected: ['a'], but gets []\n```\n\nThe issue seems to affect both `type` and `instance_of` parameters in the Check constructor, where the validation logic appears to be using the wrong parameter values internally."
  }
